title: Proposition 13
---
order: 13
---
short_label: IV.13
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To inscribe a circle in a given equilateral and equiangular pentagon.
----
proof:

Let *ABCDE* be the given equilateral and equiangular pentagon.

It is required to inscribe a circle in the pentagon *ABCDE.*

Bisect the angles *BCD* and *CDE* by the straight lines *CF* and *DF* respectively.  Join the straight lines *FB, FA,* and *FE* from the point *F* at which the straight lines *CF* and *DF* meet one another. [!just I.9]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="320" height="310" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.13 diagram" src="propIV13.gif"/></noscript>
